1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,638
In this lesson, you'll connect your
Google or Outlook calendar to Kyntlo.

2
00:00:04,638 --> 00:00:08,549
Once it's done, your bookings appear
in the calendar you already use,

3
00:00:08,549 --> 00:00:10,816
and you'll never be double-booked again.

4
00:00:11,669 --> 00:00:12,327
Why bother?

5
00:00:12,327 --> 00:00:17,293
Without a connection, Kyntlo can't see the
dentist's appointment you put in Google,

6
00:00:17,293 --> 00:00:21,482
or the school run in Outlook, so a
patient could book that exact time.

7
00:00:21,482 --> 00:00:23,995
Go to Calendar Settings, then Connections.

8
00:00:24,845 --> 00:00:26,431
Connections are personal.

9
00:00:26,431 --> 00:00:31,251
Each team member connects their own
calendar, while logged in as themselves.

10
00:00:31,251 --> 00:00:35,628
Sarah's Google Calendar is already
connected, along with Google Meet.

11
00:00:35,628 --> 00:00:38,990
Ask every team member to do
this in their first week.

12
00:00:39,839 --> 00:00:44,229
Sarah also uses Outlook for her
personal life, so let's add that too.

13
00:00:44,229 --> 00:00:47,473
Click Connect, sign in with
your Microsoft account,

14
00:00:47,473 --> 00:00:50,082
and allow Kyntlo to access your calendar.

15
00:00:50,931 --> 00:00:53,320
Now the important part: configuration.

16
00:00:53,320 --> 00:00:55,897
The linked calendar is your two-way sync.

17
00:00:55,897 --> 00:00:58,411
Every new Kyntlo booking is added to it,

18
00:00:58,411 --> 00:01:02,120
and anything you put in it
blocks your Kyntlo availability.

19
00:01:02,120 --> 00:01:04,446
Choose the calendar you use for work.

20
00:01:05,295 --> 00:01:08,429
Conflict calendars are only
checked for busy times.

21
00:01:08,429 --> 00:01:10,149
Kyntlo never writes to them.

22
00:01:10,149 --> 00:01:13,345
Tick your family calendar
and your Outlook calendar,

23
00:01:13,345 --> 00:01:17,892
so private plans block bookings, without
patients ever seeing the details.

24
00:01:18,742 --> 00:01:21,946
Leave out calendars that
don't reflect your own time,

25
00:01:21,946 --> 00:01:25,875
like a public holidays calendar
or a colleague's shared calendar.

26
00:01:25,875 --> 00:01:29,926
Otherwise, their events could block
slots you're actually free for.

27
00:01:30,775 --> 00:01:31,438
Click Save.

28
00:01:31,438 --> 00:01:34,994
From now on, Kyntlo keeps
everything in sync automatically,

29
00:01:34,994 --> 00:01:37,224
and you can see when it last checked.

30
00:01:37,224 --> 00:01:40,298
New bookings will show up
in Google within moments.

31
00:01:41,148 --> 00:01:43,615
Here's what two-way
sync means in practice.

32
00:01:43,615 --> 00:01:47,631
When a patient books, the appointment
appears in your linked calendar,

33
00:01:47,631 --> 00:01:48,549
with their name.

34
00:01:48,549 --> 00:01:53,369
When you add a lunch meeting in Google,
that time disappears from your booking page.

35
00:01:53,369 --> 00:01:57,270
And if you move a Kyntlo appointment,
the event in Google moves too.

36
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:01,384
Changed your email address,
or leaving the business?

37
00:02:01,384 --> 00:02:05,840
Use the three-dot menu next to a
connection to manage or disconnect it.

38
00:02:05,840 --> 00:02:09,731
Your existing Kyntlo appointments
stay exactly where they are.

39
00:02:10,580 --> 00:02:12,584
One last check: your time zone.

40
00:02:12,584 --> 00:02:16,333
Open Preferences, and make
sure it matches where you work.

41
00:02:16,333 --> 00:02:18,401
For Bloom, that's Europe/London.

42
00:02:18,401 --> 00:02:22,797
If the time zones don't match,
synced events can appear an hour out.

43
00:02:23,646 --> 00:02:28,730
While you're here, connect Zoom or Google
Meet if you offer online consultations.

44
00:02:28,730 --> 00:02:32,245
Then choose it as the meeting
location in your calendar,

45
00:02:32,245 --> 00:02:36,011
and Kyntlo adds a unique video
link to every online booking.

46
00:02:36,861 --> 00:02:37,934
Here's a pro tip.

47
00:02:37,934 --> 00:02:39,448
Test the sync both ways.

48
00:02:39,448 --> 00:02:44,496
Add a busy event in Google, and check
that the time disappears from your booking

49
00:02:44,496 --> 00:02:44,812
page.

50
00:02:44,812 --> 00:02:49,292
Then book a test appointment in
Kyntlo, and check it appears in Google.

51
00:02:50,148 --> 00:02:50,991
You're synced!

52
00:02:50,991 --> 00:02:55,811
In the next lesson, we'll manage appointments
day to day: booking, rescheduling,

53
00:02:55,811 --> 00:02:57,799
cancelling and handling no-shows.

54
00:02:57,799 --> 00:02:58,643
See you there.
